  "extraction_notes": "The product 9 is the Michael addition product of pyrrolidine 8 to the enone 7. The header scheme provides general conditions, while the table entries 1-10 optimize concentration, amount of 4A molecular sieves (MS), and reaction time. Yields in the table are relative to the amine 8 (footnote a). The 4A molecular sieves were powdered and dried at 100 °C (footnote b). Entry 5 and 6 appear identical in the provided crop (both 1.0 M, 0.5 g MS, 18 h, 25% yield), possibly representing a reproducibility test. Structure 9 is drawn as a saturated species with an implied chiral center, consistent with an asymmetric Michael addition."
